    "statement": "At the official rate-half scale, take e=N/8 and d=e-t_XR-1. A bipartite pair-choice construction from a binary code of length N/4 and distance t_XR+1 gives more than 16N^3 abstract pairs (P,Q) with |P|=|Q|=e and changed-set intersections at most e+d. The parameters satisfy e=t_XR+d+1 and 4e^2<=N(e+d). These are not asserted to be locator incidences. Therefore the remaining Johnson-nonpositive wedge cannot be closed from the changed-set intersection cap and row arithmetic alone.",
